Subject: include/internal/sockets.h: pull in <sys/select.h> on Unix

Several apps/ TUs (apps.c, s_server.c, s_client.c, speed.c, ocsp.c)
use fd_set / FD_ZERO / FD_SET / select via the shared
include/internal/sockets.h umbrella but the umbrella never includes
<sys/select.h>.  On glibc / BSD libc sys/types.h or sys/socket.h
re-export the symbols transitively; substrate keeps the POSIX
header layout strict (a transitive include between sys/time.h and
sys/select.h creates mutual recursion).  Pull the header in
explicitly in the Unix branch.

---
diff -urN a/include/internal/sockets.h b/include/internal/sockets.h
--- a/include/internal/sockets.h
+++ b/include/internal/sockets.h
@@ -89,6 +89,7 @@
 #   include <netinet/in.h>
 #   include <arpa/inet.h>
 #   include <netinet/tcp.h>
+#   include <sys/select.h>
 #  endif

 #  ifdef OPENSSL_SYS_AIX
